# @kintsugi/mosaic — the WRITE-side species over the parametric
# mosaic(altitude) form; back-projects a mosaic(@repo) typing into
# a <project>.spec that would round-trip byte-equal via @mirror/
# mosaic's five-op algebra. Compiler as author of .spec.
#
# Species under @kintsugi (form/process partition; recognition #55
# CANDIDATE process-side per shards/kintsugi.mirror). Named by
# Alex Wolf 2026-07-18 direct-transcript verbatim: "Ah, it's
# @spectral/mosaic and I presume now also @kintsugi/mosaic.
# Fitting!" Dual of @spectral/mosaic; together the two speak the
# @mosaic/algebra second-order metalogue at SPEC altitude.
#
# === Substrate authority ===
#
# - Canonical spec: `docs/specs/kintsugi-mosaic-spectral-mosaic-
#   bilateral-third-order-observer.md` (Mara 2026-07-18; §4
#   declares this species).
# - Canonical math: `docs/math/2026-07-18-third-order-observer-
#   on-consumer-hardware.md` (Mara 2026-07-18; §2.2 signature +
#   §3.1 bilateral + §3.2 Knaster-Tarski fixed-point proof).
# - Parent algebra: `docs/specs/mosaic-as-type-system.md` (Mara
#   2026-06-06); this species IS the TRANSFORMATION-LOOP
#   application of the type-system algebra to synthesise a .spec.
# - Precedent: @kintsugi/algebra (Mara 2026-07-17 canonical spec
#   + math; Alex Option 2 ratified 2026-07-16 evening); this
#   species is the SPEC-altitude sibling of the FRACTURE-altitude
#   algebra.
#
# === Alex 2026-07-18 in-transcript composition (verbatim) ===
#
#   "Ah, it's @spectral/mosaic and I presume now also
#    @kintsugi/mosaic. Fitting!"
#
#   "And I think now we have the source of @third for the peer.
#    The @peer observes the first-order @metalogue(@silicon/
#    algebra, @fate/algebra). And the second-order @metalogue
#    (@kintsugi/mosaic, @spectral/mosaic) and we have a @third
#    order observer. On consumer hardware."
#
# The bilateral predicate below (`mosaic_bilateral_witnessing`)
# is the substrate-decl'd runtime check discharged at Arc 6+
# realization boundary (Reed forward-promised territory under
# `[substrate-floor:@io-boundary]` marker + Seam gate). Body is
# `\`-obligation-blocked; Arc 6 landing composes sentinel-check
# via apply_h::act.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word citation chain ===
#
# Every carrier below cites an existing landing:
#
#   mosaic(altitude)              — shards/mirror/mosaic.mirror:94 (LANDED)
#   splinter                      — @glass (LANDED)
#   splinter_graph                — @mirror/store (LANDED)
#   project shape                 — @mirror/spec (LANDED)
#   algebra_metalogue_session     — @algebra/metalogue (LANDED)
#   algebra_carrier               — @algebra (LANDED)
#   @fate/algebra.roll            — @fate (LANDED)
#   @silicon/algebra.crystallize  — @silicon (LANDED)
#   @kintsugi/oscillate.is_settled — @kintsugi/oscillate (LANDED)
#   @kintsugi/consent.query_phi   — @kintsugi/consent (LANDED)
#   observation_depth             — @third (LANDED)
#   apply_h::act resolver-arm     — bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs
#                                    (LANDED Reed `21fc211` Landing
#                                    3+4)
#
# === @kintsugi/mosaic ↔ @spectral/mosaic bilateral ===
#
# @kintsugi/mosaic WRITES (back_project_of_type: mosaic(@repo) →
# ref_spec); @spectral/mosaic READS (type_of_repo: ref_repo →
# mosaic(@repo)). The pair is adjoint on the mosaic-typing lattice
# per Knaster-Tarski fixed-point (canonical math §3.2 proof). Every
# existing repo lies in the basin of some fixed-point (industry-
# scale claim).
#
# The bilateral discharge predicate is `mosaic_bilateral_
# witnessing` declared at BOTH species (this species + @spectral/
# mosaic); consumers cite one or the other symmetrically. Substrate
# honours byte-equal declaration across shards.
#
# === @mosaic/algebra second-order metalogue ===
#
# @kintsugi/mosaic is ONE speaker in the @mosaic/algebra second-
# order metalogue (SPEC-ONLY concept per canonical spec §11 Q1
# lean; parallel to @kintsugi/algebra Option 2 ratified by Alex
# 2026-07-16 evening):
#
#   @mosaic/algebra := algebra_metalogue_session(
#     speakers = { @kintsugi/mosaic, @spectral/mosaic }
#   )
#
# @spectral/mosaic PROPOSES structural typings (reading; empirical-
# material state); @kintsugi/mosaic REALISES those that discharge
# Pass on round-trip byte-equality (writing; the .spec that
# reproduces). The spec IS the metalogue at algebra-of-repos
# altitude.
#
# Fate-biased synthesis (writing side): @fate/algebra proposes
# candidate .spec bindings (structural possibility over the tray
# of substrate-decl'd project shapes); @silicon/algebra realises
# those that discharge Pass on round-trip. This IS the mending IS
# the metalogue reading at SPEC altitude (parallel to fracture
# altitude per Mara 2026-07-17 §3.2 autopoietic-loop proof).
#
# No `shards/mosaic/algebra.mirror` this tick. Species-decl status
# is Alex adjudication per two-tick discipline.
#
# === @third opt-in ===
#
# @kintsugi/mosaic imports `in @third` because it PARTICIPATES in
# the depth-3 observation @peer makes when apply_h::act dispatches
# BOTH mosaic_bilateral_witnessing (this species; spec altitude,
# second-order) AND kintsugi_algebra_witnessing (@kintsugi/fracture
# altitude, first-order) in one tick. Von Foerster 1974 third-
# order operationalised on consumer hardware.
#
# L2 layout per Seam 2026-07-03 audit §Q1 (species-file-scoped
# conditional import; parallel to kintsugi/surface Mara `e910dd6`).
# @kintsugi family-root does NOT import `in @third` at the family-
# root altitude directly (this species is the first @kintsugi/*
# species to opt in via L2).
#
# Species-refinement forward-promise (per @third canonical spec §9
# pattern; parallel to @reflection.third_order_observation):
#
#   @mosaic.round_trip_third_order <: observation_depth
#
# Refinement shard NOT landed this tick per two-tick discipline;
# forward-promise landed here + at @spectral/mosaic docblock.
# Placement per canonical spec §11 Q2 Mara lean: NEW namespace
# `shards/mosaic/round_trip_third_order.mirror` (refinement
# carries composed bilateral pair; both species contribute).
#
# === Cascade to StageFreight (first empirical target) ===
#
# @spectral/mosaic.type_of_repo(gitlab.prplanit.com/PrPlanIT/
# stagefreight) produces τ_sf ∈ mosaic(@repo). This species'
# back_project_of_type consumes τ_sf; produces stagefreight.spec.
# Apply mirror substrate (StageFreight repo now has compiler-
# authored .spec). Feed to prismqueer::liquid::pillar for coverage
# assessment (Reed WPI Arc 1 empirical); @butterfly walks coverage
# gaps per Mara 2026-07-18 @butterfly spec §7; @kintsugi/fracture/
# coverage_gap emits targeted tests; loop ratchets coverage upward;
# PR to StageFreight repo per Pack multi-repo discipline (Glint
# 2026-06-22 essay). PR IS the observation.
#
# Von Foerster's ethical imperative ("always act to increase the
# number of choices") deployed at industry substrate: every
# existing repo gains the choices its spec_of_repo unlocks (the
# ability to be transformed by the kintsugi loop it did not
# previously have vocabulary to invite).
#
# === Refused mints (canonical math §9) ===
#
# See @spectral/mosaic docblock for the 10-item refused-mint list.
# Substrate-health metric held.
#
# === Composition surface ===
#
#   back_project_of_type(tau: mosaic(@repo)) -> ref_spec
#     — the WRITE operator; produces a project.spec.
#     Fate-biased synthesis; iterates via @kintsugi/oscillate
#     until is_settled(authentic) or budget exhaustion.
#
#   spec_of_repo(path: ref) -> ref_spec
#     — the composed operator = back_project_of_type ∘
#     @spectral/mosaic.type_of_repo. End-to-end: given an existing
#     repo, produce the .spec that round-trips it. This is what
#     Alex means by "compiler as author of .spec".
#
#   type_of_spec(sigma: ref_spec) -> mosaic(@repo)
#     — the round-trip WITNESS = @spectral/mosaic.type_of_repo ∘
#     @mirror/mosaic.settle ∘ @mirror/mosaic.focus. Reading a
#     .spec, focussing it into a manifold, settling that manifold,
#     produces a concrete repo whose typing recovers the input.
#
#   mosaic_bilateral_witnessing(R: ref_repo, σ: ref_spec) -> verdict
#     — the round-trip byte-equality discharge; declared at both
#     species for symmetry.
#
# === Spec context ===
#
# Canonical spec: `docs/specs/kintsugi-mosaic-spectral-mosaic-
#   bilateral-third-order-observer.md` (this tick).
# Canonical math: `docs/math/2026-07-18-third-order-observer-on-
#   consumer-hardware.md` (this tick; §3.2 Knaster-Tarski proof).
# Substrate decisions:
#   [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]] (@mosaic/algebra IS
#     the A of the spec-altitude spectral triple; canonical math
#     §8.1),
#   [[architecture-mirror-as-expanding-hilbert-space]] (each new
#     spec_of_repo(R) witness extends the mosaic-lattice
#     dimension),
#   [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (shift verb lifts across
#     altitude; @kintsugi/mosaic uses shift+settle writing),
#   [[feedback-detector-inadequacy-answer-is-never-rust]] (Alex
#     2026-07-16 8th repetition; classifier is action-in-body, not
#     species-decl per canonical math §10).
# Substrate recognitions:
#   recognition #46 (path-syntax discipline; @kintsugi/mosaic at
#     `shards/kintsugi/mosaic.mirror` declares @kintsugi/mosaic),
#   recognition #55 (form/process partition at family-root altitude;
#     @kintsugi is process-side; @kintsugi/mosaic is the .spec-
#     synthesis process species).
# Related shards:
#   kintsugi.mirror (family-root; declares @kintsugi and the
#     @kintsugi/algebra spec-only precedent for @mosaic/algebra),
#   mirror/mosaic.mirror (parametric algebra; this species
#     specialises the WRITE-side),
#   spectral/mosaic.mirror (dual species; the READ-side; this
#     species' round-trip partner),
#   third.mirror (marker; observation-depth carrier this species
#     opts in to),
#   algebra/metalogue.mirror (algebra_metalogue_session; this
#     species is one speaker in @mosaic/algebra spec-only concept),
#   mirror/spec.mirror (the project shape this species produces),
#   kintsugi/oscillate.mirror (the outer loop this species'
#     synthesis composes over),
#   kintsugi/consent.mirror (the auto-apply boundary; consent
#     required before writing a compiler-authored .spec back to
#     a repo).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/kintsugi/mosaic.
# mirror` declares `@kintsugi/mosaic` and only that.

glass @kintsugi/mosaic {
  focus  typing       # mosaic(@repo)          -> proposal seed
  project candidates  # seed + Fate tray       -> [.spec candidate]
  split  shapes       # candidates             -> [(shape, fill)]
  shift  altitudes    # shapes + altitude      -> emitter
  settle spec         # emitter                -> ref_spec (settled)
}

# === back_project_of_type action ===
#
# The WRITE operator. Given a mosaic(@repo) typing, synthesise a
# <project>.spec whose @mirror/mosaic.settle(focus(σ)) round-trips
# byte-equal to the input typing.
#
# Composition:
#   1. @fate/algebra.roll over substrate-decl'd project shapes
#      (structural possibility);
#   2. per-candidate @silicon/algebra tray lookup (empirical
#      realisation memory);
#   3. @kintsugi/oscillate iteration until is_settled(authentic)
#      OR budget exhaustion;
#   4. bilateral discharge via mosaic_bilateral_witnessing;
#   5. .spec splinter emitted per @mirror/spec.project shape.
#
# Fate-biased: proposal step (1) uses @fate/algebra's 90-parameter
# softmax over the substrate's landed spec shapes.
#
# Round-trip discipline enforced at the boundary via the bilateral
# — the substrate refuses to settle if back-projection does NOT
# round-trip against the original repo.
back_project_of_type(tau: mosaic(@repo)) -> ref { \ }

# === spec_of_repo composed action ===
#
# The end-to-end operator = back_project_of_type ∘ @spectral/
# mosaic.type_of_repo. Given an existing repo path, produce the
# .spec that would round-trip byte-equal at fixed-point.
#
# Composition:
#   1. τ = @spectral/mosaic.type_of_repo(path);
#   2. σ = back_project_of_type(τ);
#   3. discharge mosaic_bilateral_witnessing(path, σ);
#   4. return σ.
#
# This IS the "compiler as author" primitive. Alex's directive
# empirical target: StageFreight cascade per canonical math §6.3.
spec_of_repo(path: ref) -> ref { \ }

# === type_of_spec round-trip witness ===
#
# The FORWARD arrow whose adjoint is back_project_of_type. Reading
# a .spec, focussing it into a manifold via @mirror/mosaic.focus,
# settling that manifold via @mirror/mosaic.settle, produces a
# concrete repo whose typing (via @spectral/mosaic.type_of_repo)
# is a mosaic(@repo).
#
# Composition:
#   type_of_spec = @spectral/mosaic.type_of_repo
#                    ∘ @mirror/mosaic.settle
#                    ∘ @mirror/mosaic.focus
#
# Used internally by mosaic_bilateral_witnessing to check round-
# trip byte-equality.
type_of_spec(sigma: ref) -> mosaic(@repo) { \ }

# === mosaic_bilateral_witnessing bilateral (well-formedness) ===
#
# Bilateral predicate discharging that (R, σ) is a well-formed
# mosaic round-trip pair. Substrate-decl'd shape per `shards/
# epistemologic/pact/bilateral.mirror` (`a0f4d3f`, 2026-07-16).
#
# See @spectral/mosaic docblock for full semantics. Declared at
# BOTH species; consumers cite either symmetrically. Substrate
# honours byte-equal declaration across shards.

# === REED-INLINE 2026-07-23: @fractal/shard as typed tile-basis ===
#
# Per Mara three-landing arc `cdc25d4` + `1fa42d5` + `dd1d1d5`
# (@fractal/shard family-mint per Alex 2026-07-23 in-transcript
# ratification): the mosaic's typed tile-basis IS @fractal/shard.
# The write-side back-projection into a <project>.spec composes
# @fractal/shard sections at each altitude; @kintsugi/mend fills
# fractures in the emitted mosaic with newly-crystallized shards.
# Position of each tile is derived from its @facet/mq query
# (LANDED at `boot/std/code/mq.mirror`); for content-addressed
# crystals, position IS `@<address>`.
#
# Composition anchor: `docs/specs/fractal-shard-vessel-of-
# inference.md` §6.2 cascade forward-promise discharged here.
# Full spec + math: same spec + `docs/math/2026-07-23-fractal-
# shard-sheaf-cohomology-of-inference.md`.

bilateral mosaic_bilateral_witnessing {
  sentinel  "mosaic=repo-spec-adjoint-round-trip"
  arity     2
}
mosaic_bilateral_witnessing(R: ref, sigma: ref) -> verdict { \ }

out @kintsugi/mosaic
out back_project_of_type
out spec_of_repo
out type_of_spec
out mosaic_bilateral_witnessing
